.I /usr/local/bfd/alert/custom.d/
User template overrides (per-file, preserved across upgrades).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/rules/
Service rule files (57 rules).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/tmp/pressure.dat
Pressure scoring workspace (timestamp, IP, service, weight). Pruned every ~10 half-lives.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/tmp/bans.active
Currently active bans.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/tmp/bans.history
Historical ban/unban records.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/stats/attack.pool
Threat activity pool \(em unified event store recording all detected auth
failures (ban, escalate, observed) and outcomes.
10-field format: timestamp, IP, service, count, country, action, duration,
ports, pressure, trip type.
Sub-trip observations (ACTION=observed) are recorded alongside ban decisions
so event history persists across pressure decay cycles.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/ignore.hosts
User-managed IP ignore list.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bfd/exclude.files
List of files containing hosts to ignore.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/bfd
Cron job (batch mode, every 2 minutes).
.TP
.I /etc/cron.daily/bfd
Daily maintenance (state rotation, cleanup).
.TP
.I /etc/logrotate.d/bfd
Log rotation configuration (copytruncate, weekly).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bfd-watch.service
Systemd unit for watch mode (recommended).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bfd.service
Systemd unit for batch mode.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bfd.timer
Systemd timer for batch mode (alternative to cron).
.TP
.I /etc/init.d/bfd-watch
SysVinit init script for watch mode (CentOS 6/7, Ubuntu 14.04).
.TP
.I /etc/bash_completion.d/bfd
Bash tab completion for bfd commands.
.TP
.I /var/log/bfd_log
Application log.
.SH UPGRADING
When upgrading from a previous BFD installation (including v1.5\-2),
.B install.sh
automatically backs up the existing installation to
.I /usr/local/bfd.bk.DDMMYYYY\-HHMMSS
(symlinked as
.IR /usr/local/bfd.bk.last )
and runs
.B importconf
to merge configuration and preserve state.
.PP
.B importconf
migrates: user configuration (conf.bfd values), legacy variable name
translations (TRIG \(-> PRESSURE_TRIP, BAN_DURATION \(-> BAN_TTL, etc.),
per\-rule overrides (thresholds.conf \(-> pressure.conf), firewall backend
detection, ban state (bans.active, bans.history, pressure.dat), attack pool
(attack.pool), log tracking state (tlog byte\-offsets, journal cursors),
user\-customized alert template partials, and ignore lists.
.PP
.B Note:
In 2.0.1, the internal pressure workspace was renamed from
.I events.dat
to
.IR pressure.dat .
.B importconf
handles this automatically \(em if the backup contains
.I events.dat
but not
.IR pressure.dat ,
the file is migrated under the new name.
.PP
Post\-upgrade verification:
.RS 4
.nf
bfd \-c          # health check and diagnostics
bfd \-\-status    # show current ban/event summary
.fi
.RE
.PP
To roll back, flush any new bans and restore the backup:
.RS 4
.nf
bfd \-\-flush\-all
rm \-rf /usr/local/bfd
cp \-a /usr/local/bfd.bk.last /usr/local/bfd
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
In watch mode
.RB ( "bfd \-w" ):
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration (conf.bfd, internals.conf, pressure.conf)
without restarting.
.TP
.B SIGTERM\fR, \fBSIGINT
Clean shutdown: release lock, exit gracefully.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error (invalid config, unknown option).
.TP
.B 2
Lock error (another instance running).
.TP
.B 3
Prerequisite error (missing tlog, rules directory, etc.).
